Aerie-Purpose: Leave the WebUI test libraries that do not build against Helium's patched WebUI sources (cr_elements, settings, signin, history, new_tab_page, customize_chrome, extensions) out of the webui-test resource bundle.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/test/data/webui/BUILD.gn (test-only code)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Chromium's WebUI tests for these pages call APIs that Helium changed or removed
(AvatarIcon.isCustomAvatar, getAvailableIcons, the searchbox and
searchedImageButton elements, the sync entries in the history and extensions
sidebars, the About page's update status), so their build_ts targets fail.
settings and cr_elements fail together: the settings tests import cr_elements.
Aerie's UI tests use none of them. Fixing them means patching .ts files, but
the build fetches those files after the patches apply, so the test-only fix is
to leave the libraries out of the bundle that webui_test_resources builds.
Test-only: nothing in the shipped browser links it. Issue #175.

